    "https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/6928": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor Pool, Manufacturing & Mechanical Engineering Technology (MMET)",
      "description": "Oregon Institute of Technology Portal | Adjunct Instructor Pool, Manufacturing &amp; Mechanical Engineering Technology (MMET) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs Campus Locations Human Resources Oregon Tech Adjunct Instructor Pool, Manufacturing & Mechanical Engineering Technology (MMET) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please submit an application and include the following elements: Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Transcripts (Unofficial) Teaching Philosophy License/Certification Other Document Posting Details Position Details Position Type Adjunct Working Title Adjunct Instructor Pool, Manufacturing & Mechanical Engineering Technology (MMET) Classification Title Adjunct Faculty College/Division College of Engr, Tech & Mgmt (ETM) Department Manufacturing & Mechanical Eng Tech Hiring Unit Work Location Appointment FTE (%) Position Terms/Mo Full/Part time Annual Salary Based on WLU Position Summary Department Summary Manufacturing Engineering Technology The objective of the Manufacturing Engineering Technology undergraduate program is to offer students a quality education that provides the greatest possible opportunity for rewarding and successful careers. This includes practical training and technical education in engineering, manufacturing processes, and manufacturing equipment as well as supplemental coursework in communications, mathematics, science, social science, and business. Mechanical Engineering The Mechanical Engineering Program at Oregon Institute of Technology provides an excellent theoretical and applied or hands on engineering education. The program provides graduates with a foundation in fundamentals, applications, design, project management, communications, and professional and ethical responsibility. Mechanical Engineering Technology The objective of the Mechanical Engineering Technology Program is to ensure that graduates of this curriculum acquire competency in those theoretical, applied engineering and practical subjects necessary to become successful in their careers. The program strives to maintain a reputation for academic standards that will assure graduates a welcome by prospective employers. https://www.oit.edu/mmet Position Summary The Department of Manufacturing and Mechanical Engineering Technology at Oregon Institute of Technology (Oregon Tech) is seeking applications for a part-time adjunct faculty pool for the 2025-2026 academic year. These positions will be based at the Portland-Metro campus in Wilsonville and will be offered on a term-by-term basis. Renewals may be considered annually at the discretion of the department chair. Adjunct faculty will be responsible for developing and/or teaching undergraduate courses within the Manufacturing and Mechanical Engineering Technology department, which is part of the College of Engineering, Technology, and Management at Oregon Tech. Courses that may require instructors include: Automation and Robotics Programmable Logic Controllers (PLCs) Control Systems Materials Science and Engineering Mechanical Vibrations Electric Power Systems Machining Processes Manufacturing Tool Design Computer-Aided Design ( CAD ) / Computer-Aided Manufacturing ( CAM ) Minimum Requirements Additional Requirements Proven track record of teaching engineering courses. Education must include (at least) a Master’s degree in an engineering discipline by the start date of employment. Successful candidates must hold permanent, full-time, US Work Authorization. Preferred Qualifications PhD in an engineering dicipline. Application Information Recruitment Type External Application Screening Begins 05/07/2025 Job Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicant Please submit an application and include the following elements: Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Transcripts (Unofficial) Teaching Philosophy License/Certification Other Document Background/Pre-Employment Check Any offer of employment to a successful candidate will be conditioned upon the University’s receipt of a satisfactory background check, motor vehicle check, physical abilities check, and/or any other conditions of employment contained in the vacancy announcement. AA/EEO Statement Oregon Tech is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Educator and Employer. The University does not discriminate in access to its educational programs and activities, or with respect to hiring, or the terms and conditions of employment, on the basis of age, color, disability, marital status, national origin, race, religion or creed, sex or gender, gender identity or gender expression, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other basis in law. Oregon Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact the Office of Human Resource at 541-885-1028 or oithr@oit.edu . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Transcripts (Unofficial) Teaching Philosophy License/Certification Other Document Contact Us: Office of Human Resources 3201 Campus Dr. Klamath Falls, Oregon 97601 Phone: (541) 885-1120 Email: oithr@oit.edu Website: http://www.oit.edu/hr Policies | Campus Safety | Campus Alerts | Directory | Site Index Connect with us: | | To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7428": {
      "title": "Student Involvement & Belonging Coordinator",
      "description": "Oregon Institute of Technology Portal | Student Involvement &amp; Belonging Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs Campus Locations Human Resources Oregon Tech Student Involvement & Belonging Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The initial review of applications will begin June 22, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the initial review date until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. Therefore, at the discretion of the University, materials received after the initial review date may not receive full consideration. Required Documents Resume Cover Letter For additional information or support, please contact the Office of Human Resources: oithr@oit.edu Posting Details Position Details Position Type Administrative Working Title Student Involvement & Belonging Coordinator Classification Title Coordinator College/Division Student Affairs Department Student Involvement & Belonging Hiring Unit Work Location Klamath Falls Appointment FTE (%) 1.00 Position Terms/Mo 12 Full/Part time Full Time Annual Salary $45,400 – $55,600 Position Summary Department Summary Figuring out how to spend your time doesn’t have to be rocket science, but it can be: Some of our students do build rockets for fun. But there’s also no one, singular Oregon Tech experience. Our campuses bring collective energy into one community where you’ll find gamers and geeks (proudly), explorers of the natural world, athletes, book aficionados and volunteers passionate about changing the world through causes they believe in. Our students are innovators— like our female engineers who created technology that turns waste plastic back into crude oil . They are difference makers like the dental hygiene students who traveled to Jamaica to provide dental care to rural areas. And about those rocket scientists? Our students have worked with NASA to launch stuff into space. At our Klamath Falls campus, entirely heated by geothermal water resources, you’ll find students living, eating, and working together, allowing them to build long-term personal and professional connections. Outside the classroom, they lead student government, exercise in our campus facilities, and challenge one another in eSports. They also volunteer and engage in our wide range of student organizations—or, when they can’t find exactly what they’re looking for, they create their own. https://www.oit.edu/campus-life Position Summary The Student Involvement & Belonging ( SIB ) Coordinator creates and supports a holistic student experience responsible for supporting the vision, initiatives, programs, and daily operations for Klamath Falls students. The SIB Coordinator will co-lead Klamath Falls campus Student Involvement & Belonging programs and initiatives; collaborating with partners across the university campus to ensure a student0centered approach to the creation and implementation of programming that enhances a student’s sense of belonging and increases student’s leadership development and cultural competency. The SIB Coordinator will use research, data, and assessment to lead the university in developing and implementing a co-curricular journey in which student’s belonging and leadership development experience will be enhanced. The SIB Coordinator is responsible for the Klamath Falls student involvement and campus activities through providing advising and support for Registered Student Organizations, creating Klamath Falls campus-wide student engagement opportunities, such as large-scale social events including Music Garden. The SIB Coordinator will develop, student leadership and cultural competency development, and diversity and belonging programming; and support the operations and programming of Student Involvement & Belonging in collaboration with the Director of SIB and Assistant Director of SIB (Portland-Metro). Student Involvement & Belonging provides programs and services students need to achieve academic, personal, and professional goals. We provide programs, services, and partners with other divisions to provide support, enhance personal wellness, develop leadership and communication skills, and promote a strong sense of community. We encourage students to get involved on campus, approach faculty and staff with ideas, questions and concerns and take advantage of the resources that will help them succeed. Minimum Requirements Additional Requirements Bachelor’s Degree with one (1) year of professional experience. Any combination of relevant education and experience may be substituted for the educational requirement on a year-for-year basis. Experience working with any combination of student organizations, student leadership, orientation programs, campus activities, diversity awareness, a multicultural office, cultural programming, or with diverse populations. Ability to work, communicate, and collaborate in diverse, multicultural, and inclusive settings effectively and respectfully. Excellent interpersonal communication and oral presentation skills. Excellent professional writing skills. Preferred Qualifications Two (2) or more years of experience in higher education institutions, event management, and/or driving student engagement through technology. Strong customer service orientation. One (1) or more years supervising and/or advising student staff. Application Information Recruitment Type External Application Screening Begins 06/22/2026 Job Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicant The initial review of applications will begin June 22, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the initial review date until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. Therefore, at the discretion of the University, materials received after the initial review date may not receive full consideration. Required Documents Resume Cover Letter For additional information or support, please contact the Office of Human Resources: oithr@oit.edu Background/Pre-Employment Check Any offer of employment to a successful candidate will be conditioned upon the University’s receipt of a satisfactory background check, motor vehicle check, physical abilities check, and/or any other conditions of employment contained in the vacancy announcement. AA/EEO Statement Oregon Tech is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Educator and Employer. The University does not discriminate in access to its educational programs and activities, or with respect to hiring, or the terms and conditions of employment, on the basis of age, color, disability, marital status, national origin, race, religion or creed, sex or gender, gender identity or gender expression, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other basis in law. Oregon Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact the Office of Human Resource at 541-885-1028 or oithr@oit.edu . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document Contact Us: Office of Human Resources 3201 Campus Dr. Klamath Falls, Oregon 97601 Phone: (541) 885-1120 Email: oithr@oit.edu Website: http://www.oit.edu/hr Policies | Campus Safety | Campus Alerts | Directory | Site Index Connect with us: | | To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
