    "https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7492": {
      "title": "Residence Life Coordinator",
      "description": "Oregon Institute of Technology Portal | Residence Life Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs Campus Locations Human Resources Oregon Tech Residence Life Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The initial review of applications will begin September 14, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the initial review date until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. Therefore, at the discretion of the University, materials received after the initial review date may not receive full consideration. Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Other Document For additional information or support, please contact the Office of Human Resources: oithr@oit.edu Posting Details Position Details Position Type Administrative Working Title Residence Life Coordinator Classification Title Coordinator College/Division Student Affairs Department Housing Hiring Unit Work Location Klamath Falls Appointment FTE (%) 100 Position Terms/Mo 12 month Full/Part time Full Time Annual Salary $42,000 – $45,000 Position Summary Department Summary The Klamath Falls campus offers two housing facilities to allow students to stay on campus as they study, which comes with a host of perks. In addition to convenience, staying on campus has been shown to improve academic success. It allows students to fully immerse themselves in the campus culture, make lasting friendships with people of diverse backgrounds, and partake in countless activities—including annual traditions such as Tech Con and Spring Fling. Late-night study sessions. Workouts in the Recreation Center. Board games in the study room. BBQs in the Quad with friends. Living on campus provides experiences that shape their time at Oregon Tech—and their future. For additional information regarding the Department of Housing and Residence Life, please visit: https://www.oit.edu/campus-life/housing Position Summary Oregon Tech Housing and Residence Life is seeking a vibrant and enthusiastic Residence Life Coordinator ( RLC ) to join the Housing and Residence Life team. The RLC serves as a key member of the Residence Life team in support of the mission, vision and values of the Housing and Residence Life department and Oregon Tech. This employee works closely with the Lead Residence Life Coordinator, student staff, and residential students daily. The work includes developing community within all housing facilities to ensure a safe and welcoming environment for residential students as well as the campus community, families and guests who interact with Housing and Residence Life. The RLC also supports and participates in Housing and Residence Life sponsored and supported programming in support of student learning initiatives. This position supervises the First Year Experience ( FYE ) student staff as well as the Student Success Mentor ( SSM ) staff team, reporting to the Assistant Director of Residence Life. This position works Monday through Friday as well as some evenings and weekends. The RLC also serves in the on-call rotation to respond to Housing and Residence Life related emergency/crisis needs after hours and on weekends. A willingness and desire to work with students as they live and learn in a residential setting is essential as well as a strong work ethic to ensure the student experience while on campus and at Oregon Tech is one filled with positive learning experiences in a safe and inclusive environment. The RLC is a live in position, with a fully furnished apartment and Meal Plan 3 included in the compensation. Minimum Requirements Additional Requirements The RLC must have an earned bachelor’s degree, and with experience working with a housing and residence life department (as a student or professional staff) A high level of knowledge working in the Microsoft suite of programs is essential. The RLC must possess quality time management skills and work with integrity. Must reside in university-provided on-campus housing for the duration of employment in this position. The successful candidate must be able to maintain an on-campus residence and be available to respond to position-related responsibilities outside of regular business hours, as required. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience supervising student staff preferred, especially if supervision involved working with a college student population. Application Information Recruitment Type External Application Screening Begins 09/14/2026 Job Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicant The initial review of applications will begin September 14, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the initial review date until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. Therefore, at the discretion of the University, materials received after the initial review date may not receive full consideration. Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Other Document For additional information or support, please contact the Office of Human Resources: oithr@oit.edu Background/Pre-Employment Check Any offer of employment to a successful candidate will be conditioned upon the University’s receipt of a satisfactory background check, motor vehicle check, physical abilities check, and/or any other conditions of employment contained in the vacancy announcement. AA/EEO Statement Oregon Tech is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Educator and Employer. The University does not discriminate in access to its educational programs and activities, or with respect to hiring, or the terms and conditions of employment, on the basis of age, color, disability, marital status, national origin, race, religion or creed, sex or gender, gender identity or gender expression, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other basis in law. Oregon Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact the Office of Human Resource at 541-885-1028 or oithr@oit.edu . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Other Document Contact Us: Office of Human Resources 3201 Campus Dr. Klamath Falls, Oregon 97601 Phone: (541) 885-1120 Email: oithr@oit.edu Website: http://www.oit.edu/hr Policies | Campus Safety | Campus Alerts | Directory | Site Index Connect with us: | | To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
